# Backend core

- Stack: ASP.NET Core Web API, **.NET 10**, EF Core 9, Pomelo MySQL, DB `demoCrudDb`.
- Architecture: **Controller → Service → DbContext** only. No repository pattern, no MediatR, no generic auth framework unless explicitly requested.
- Keep MySQL. Do not change DB provider or invent schema migrations without need.
- Prefer small, focused changes. Do not refactor unrelated files.
- Learning project: prefer clear code over clever abstractions.
- Frontend rules will be added later; do not invent FE conventions here.

## Seed / local auth

- Seeded SuperAdmin: username `superadmin`, password `Admin@123` (hash in seed only).
- JWT signing key lives in **user secrets**, never commit real keys.
- VS debug often locks `DemoCrudBackend.exe`; build to an alternate output if needed and ask the user to restart the debug session.
